                "question": "<p class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Images\" class=\"q-img\" src=\"images/t0301-01.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 10px 0; display: block;\"/></p><p class=\"noindentt\"><strong>Time:</strong> 45 minutes. You may refer to the constants sheet and the equation sheet, both of which are found in the appendix. You may use a calculator.</p><p class=\"ques\"><strong><a href=\"ch19t.xhtml#rch19p_1\" id=\"ch19p_1\">1.</a></strong> An object moves along the positive $x$-axis. The net force on the object as a function of time $t$ measured in seconds is given in newtons by the function $F$($t$) = 3$t^{2} +t$ + 2. What is the impulse delivered to the object during the first second of motion?</p>",
